```apex
/**
 * TriggerRecord implementation for the Account sObject.
 *
 * The Trigger Actions Framework (TAF) instantiates this class (via
 * TriggerRecord_Class_Name__c on the sObject_Trigger_Setting__mdt record
 * named "Account") and populates the inherited newSobject / oldSobject
 * members for each record being processed. The framework then evaluates
 * each Trigger_Action__mdt Entry_Criteria__c formula against this record:
 *
 *   - Current field values are referenced plainly, e.g. Rating
 *   - Pre-DML values are available through oldSobject, e.g. oldSobject.Rating
 *     (populated in update and delete contexts, null on insert/undelete)
 *
 * This class holds no state and performs no filtering of its own, so every
 * Account trigger context (inserts included) continues to flow to all
 * registered actions exactly as before.
 */
public inherited sharing class AccountTriggerRecord extends TriggerRecord {

    /** Convenience typed view of the record in its current (new) state. */
    public Account getNewAccount() {
        return (Account) newSobject;
    }

    /** Convenience typed view of the record as it existed before the DML. */
    public Account getOldAccount() {
        return (Account) oldSobject;
    }
}
```

